   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Start the workup to diagnose TB in the patient not needing urgent attention • Determine whether the patient has been on TB treatment and interrupted treatment for > 2 months: if DS-TB 110; if INH-resistant TB or RR-TB, refer to doctor or discuss with PCAC/NCAC 200. • Send 1 sputum sample for TB NAAT: demonstrate how to give sputum sample 105. If unable to produce sputum, induce sputum 105 and refer for chest x-ray 104. Doctor to review chest x-ray. - Ensure specimen type, site and patient details clearly indicated on request form. Indicate on the request form: patient's HIV status and whether the patient had TB in past 2 years. • Test for HIV 124. • If HIV and TB symptoms and CD4 ≤ 200 or WHO stage 3 or 4 disease, also do urine LAM test: - If LAM positive, diagnose TB on urine LAM, start DS-TB treatment same day 106 and follow up TB NAAT result. If LAM negative, manage according to TB NAAT results below. • Ask the patient to return for results after 2 days and manage further according to results below. If TB NAAT unsuccessful, send repeat sputum sample for TB NAAT.",
